      "learningTitle": "Using German Modal Verbs",
      "learningPoints": [
        "Conjugate common modal verbs such as können, müssen, wollen, dürfen and möchten.",
        "Place the conjugated modal verb in second position in a main clause.",
        "Put the main infinitive at the end of the clause.",
        "Use können for ability and dürfen for permission.",
        "Use müssen for necessity and wollen/möchten for intention or preference.",
        "Keep the main verb in infinitive form after a modal."
      ],
